# Twilight of the Union: multiplayer lobby panel in the broadcast style (full copy of vanilla 1.19.3
# interface/playerlobby.gui; every vanilla element name and type is kept). Used in the frontend lobby AND in game.
#   player_lobby_stats_window  a 24 px slate plate row (GFX_totu_mp_lobby, tools/build_mp_gfx.py) at x 181,
#                              H-148..H-124: above the frontend lobby's Back / Load plates (H-112..H-72), no longer
#                              on top of them; lower left in game as before
#   player_lobby_window        in-game board (GFX_totu_board_ig); player list and chat on raised sub-panels; info
#                              texts and Start in one row inside the bottom edge. Widths are explicit; the negative
#                              heights are tuned for "parent minus" (tools/render_gui.py): should the engine count
#                              them from the element position instead, the panels only end higher, never overlap.
